  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Reading the diagram",
      "items": [
        "Rows are physical columns: pk, fk and uk badges mark primary, foreign and unique keys; a column can carry several roles.",
        "Solid crow's-foot lines are foreign keys (many-to-one). Dashed lines are logical links without a database foreign key.",
        "The legend strip is hidden because a route ran through its band; the badges on each row carry the same information."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Invariants enforced in the schema",
      "items": [
        "ledger_transactions owns the balance CHECKs; ledger_entries cannot sum sibling rows, so it only carries UNIQUE(transaction, account).",
        "UNIQUE(source_type, source_id) makes a second ledger transaction for the same subscription or gift impossible.",
        "Partial unique index on subscriptions: one active row per (subscriber, publication)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Logical links without foreign keys",
      "items": [
        "event_processing_attempts.event_id, user_feed_events.source_event_id and reconciliation_log.event_id point at the envelope's event_id inside outbox_events.payload; no FK crosses the async boundary.",
        "ledger_transactions.source_id is polymorphic over subscriptions and gift_transactions, discriminated by source_type.",
        "subscriptions.charged_amount_cents freezes the creation charge; amount_cents mutates on tier change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Immutable tables",
      "items": [
        "ledger_transactions, ledger_entries, post_versions, reconciliation_log reject UPDATE and DELETE through a database trigger and a SQLAlchemy guard.",
        "Columns beyond the Sprint-2 migration (charged_*, next_attempt_at, terminal_at, locked_until, failure_event_emitted_at) exist in the models but their migration is not yet tracked in git."
      ]
    }
  ]
